{"status":"ok","message-type":"work","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,3,11]],"date-time":"2026-03-11T12:59:29Z","timestamp":1773233969635,"version":"3.50.1"},"reference-count":0,"publisher":"European Mathematical Society - EMS - Publishing House GmbH","issue":"3","content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["Oberwolfach Rep."],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2013,5,29]]},"abstract":"<jats:p>Optimal configurations of points arise in many contexts, for example classical ground states for interacting particle systems, Euclidean packings of convex bodies, as well as minimal discrete and continuous energy problems for general kernels. Relevant questions in this area include the understanding of asymptotic optimal configurations, of lattice and periodic configurations, the development of algorithmic constructions of near optimal configurations, and the application of methods in convex optimization such as linear and semidefinite programming.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.4171\/owr\/2012\/40","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2013,5,29]],"date-time":"2013-05-29T17:44:58Z","timestamp":1369849498000},"page":"2429-2492","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":1,"title":["Optimal and Near Optimal Configurations on Lattices and Manifolds"],"prefix":"10.4171","volume":"9","author":[{"given":"Christine","family":"Bachoc","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Universit\u00e9 de Bordeaux I, Talence, France"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Peter","family":"Grabner","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Technische Universit\u00e4t Graz, Austria"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0003-1079-9074","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Edward B.","family":"Saff","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Vanderbilt University, Nashville, USA"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}